    "guide.sick.title": "Understanding sick-leave certificates",
    "guide.sick.a": "Certificate A — employer",
    "guide.sick.aText": "Usually the first 9 days of illness. The employer calculates sick pay; a VSAA application does not cover this period.",
    "guide.sick.b": "Certificate B — VSAA",
    "guide.sick.bText": "Usually from day 10 for your own illness. The benefit is 80% of the average contribution wage and must be claimed.",
    "guide.sick.eligibility": "What are the main conditions?",
    "guide.sick.eligibilityText": "Generally, sickness-insurance contributions for 3 of the last 6 or 6 of the last 24 months. Claim within 6 months of the first day of incapacity. Exceptions apply in certain cases.",
    "guide.sick.child": "When your child is ill",
    "guide.sick.childText": "Certificate B for caring for a sick child starts on day one. Conditions vary by age, place of care and illness. See the VSAA child-care sickness benefit guidance.",
    "guide.sick.status": "What does the certificate status mean?",
    "guide.sick.statusText": "Unpaid — no application in the demo register. Submitted — your request is saved and awaits review. Granted — the demo administrator approved it; this does not confirm an actual bank transfer.",
    "guide.work.title": "Understanding social-insurance contributions",
    "guide.work.what": "What do contributions cover?",
    "guide.work.whatText": "Contributions fund social insurance, including sickness, maternity, paternity, parental, unemployment and pension coverage. The insurance categories depend on your status.",
    "guide.work.chart": "How to read this overview",
    "guide.work.chartText": "Each bar represents one of the last 16 months. Highlighted gaps indicate months without a demo contribution record. Hover over a month to see its employer or gap description.",
    "guide.work.insurance": "Contribution periods and benefit amounts",
    "guide.work.insuranceText": "The month count helps check qualification periods, but does not determine your payment amount. The average contribution wage and calculation period must be considered separately for each benefit.",
    "guide.work.unemployment": "If employment has ended",
    "guide.work.unemploymentText": "Unemployment benefit generally requires NVA unemployed status, at least 1 year of total insurance history and unemployment contributions for 12 of the last 16 months. NVA registration and a VSAA application are separate steps.",
    "guide.work.missing": "If a contribution record is missing",
    "guide.work.missingText": "Compare your pay documents with the real VSAA e-service records. Discuss discrepancies with your employer and VSAA or VID. One missing month alone does not confirm that entitlement has been lost.",
    "guide.work.demo": "What does this prototype check?",
    "guide.work.demoText": "The contribution periods and employers shown here are fictional. They are not VID or VSAA registry records. This overview does not contain lifetime insurance history or contribution amounts; its unemployment scenario is simplified for demonstration.",
